---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Community">
  <h1>Community Outreach</h1>
  <p>
    Outside the lab, I spend a lot of my time on mentoring and community
    work&mdash;it's just as much a part of who I am as the science is.
  </p>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Food Not Bombs</h3>
    <p class="pub-meta">September 2024 &ndash; Present</p>
    <p>
      I volunteer weekly with Food Not Bombs East Bay, helping serve 25&ndash;40
      meals a week to our community. It's become one of the most grounding
      parts of my week, and a direct way to put my belief in mutual aid
      into practice.
    </p>
    <a
      class="btn secondary"
      href="https://eastbayfoodnotbombs.org/"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
    >
      Visit Food Not Bombs East Bay
    </a>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Sigma Xi, the Scientific Research Honor Society</h3>

    <p style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--pink-700); margin-bottom: 0.1rem;">
      Berkeley Chapter
    </p>
    <p style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--pink-500); margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0.2rem;">
      VP and CSA Chair
    </p>
    <p class="pub-meta">September 2021 &ndash; Present</p>
    <p>
      As Vice President of the Berkeley chapter of Sigma Xi, The Scientific
      Research Honor Society, I helped build the Committee for Student
      Advancement (CSA) from the ground up&mdash;a group that grew to
      roughly 30 members and connects researchers across STEM fields who
      might otherwise never cross paths in their own buildings or
      departments. As CSA Chairperson, I led a board of about 4 members
      planning community events, and pioneered the Sigma Xi&ndash;ATP Bio
      Research Symposium &amp; Poster Session, bringing together roughly
      25 student presenters and 150 attendees around a keynote speaker.
    </p>
    <a
      class="btn secondary"
      href="https://community.sigmaxi.org/communities/allcommunities/chaptergroupdetails?CommunityKey=4d4241bc-8689-4e5f-839e-f9edcd89c314"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
    >
      Visit Sigma Xi, Berkeley Chapter
    </a>

    <p style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--pink-700); margin-top: 1.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.1rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line);">
      Northeastern University Chapter
    </p>
    <p style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--pink-500); margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0.2rem;">
      DEI Chair
    </p>
    <p class="pub-meta">July 2020 &ndash; May 2021</p>
    <p>
      As an Associate Member of the Northeastern University chapter, I
      served as Diversity &amp; Inclusion Chair, working to make the
      chapter's research community more welcoming and representative. My
      induction into Sigma Xi itself recognized independent investigation
      resulting in new scientific discoveries.
    </p>
    <a
      class="btn secondary"
      href="https://sigmaxinortheastern.sites.northeastern.edu/"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
    >
      Visit Sigma Xi, Northeastern Chapter
    </a>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>BioEHSC Academic Judge</h3>
    <p class="pub-meta">April 2022 &ndash; April 2026</p>
    <p>
      Each spring, I volunteer as an academic judge for the Bay Area
      Bioscience Education Health &amp; Science Challenge (BioEHSC), a
      full-day pitch competition for high school teams. Paired with one
      or two other judges&mdash;PhDs, PhD students, and other STEM
      professionals&mdash;I watch 10 to 15 ten-minute team pitches
      followed by Q&amp;A, assessing each team's depth of knowledge and
      offering feedback where I can. It's one of my favorite volunteer
      days of the year: I get to network with other judges and
      professionals, and watch high schoolers challenge themselves and
      come up with genuinely creative ideas.
    </p>
    <a
      class="btn secondary"
      href="https://bioehs.studentorg.berkeley.edu/bioehsc/"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
    >
      Visit BioEHSC
    </a>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Adventure Challenge Volunteer</h3>
    <p class="pub-meta">September 2018 &ndash; December 2019</p>
    <p>
      I was paired with a 13-year-old girl with autism through the
      Adventure Challenge program, planning weekly trips to the YMCA pool
      for swimming and pool games. The goal was simple but meaningful:
      promote physical activity, social interaction, and overall health and
      wellness to help her maintain a healthy, active lifestyle.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Advancement Via Individual Determination (AVID) Tutor</h3>
    <p class="pub-meta">September 2018 &ndash; December 2018</p>
    <p>
      As an AVID tutor, I served as a discussion mediator during highly
      interactive tutoring sessions, helping students learn to guide each
      other toward solutions through questions and critical thinking rather
      than direct answers. The goal was to help students build effective,
      long-term study habits and the intellectual confidence to pursue and
      succeed in higher education after graduating high school.
    </p>
    <a
      class="btn secondary"
      href="https://www.avid.org/"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
    >
      Learn about AVID
    </a>
  </div>
</Layout>
